sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant R as Router (POST /v1/items)
    participant TX as repository.transaction()
    participant PG as PostgresRepository
    participant DB as Postgres (RLS bypassed)

    rect rgb(235,245,255)
    note over R,DB: Flow A — create item (atomic spend), mirrors SqliteRepository
    R->>TX: with repository.transaction():
    TX->>DB: BEGIN
    R->>PG: get_idempotent_item(key) [optional]
    PG->>DB: SELECT item_id, job_id FROM idempotency_keys WHERE user_id=%s AND endpoint=%s AND key=%s
    DB-->>PG: (item_id, job_id) | None
    alt not a replay
        R->>PG: create_item(user_id, 'draft')
        PG->>DB: INSERT INTO items (id,user_id,status,attributes,created_at,updated_at) VALUES (...,NULL,...)
        R->>PG: create_job(item_id, user_id, kind=FULL)
        PG->>DB: INSERT INTO jobs (...,'queued',0,0.0,'stub',...)  -- provider='stub' explicit
        R->>PG: append_usage_event(UsageEventRecord item_enqueued units=-1)
        PG->>DB: INSERT INTO usage_events (user_id,event,units,...) VALUES (...,'item_enqueued',-1,...)
        R->>PG: store_idempotent_item(key)
        PG->>DB: INSERT INTO idempotency_keys (...) ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE ...
    end
    TX->>DB: COMMIT
    end

    rect rgb(255,245,235)
    note over R,DB: Flow B — job claim (the Postgres behavioral advantage: FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED)
    participant W as Worker.claim_next()
    W->>TX: with repository.transaction():
    TX->>DB: BEGIN
    W->>PG: peek_next_queued_job()
    PG->>DB: SELECT j.* FROM jobs j\n  WHERE j.state='queued'\n  AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM assets a WHERE a.item_id=j.item_id AND a.kind='source')\n  ORDER BY j.created_at, j.id\n  FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED LIMIT 1
    DB-->>PG: oldest claimable job (row locked, others skipped)
    W->>PG: apply_transition -> update_job(running)
    PG->>DB: UPDATE jobs SET state='running', ... (NO updated_at; trigger sets it) WHERE id=%s
    TX->>DB: COMMIT  -- releases the row lock
    end
    note right of DB: SQLite uses 'begin immediate' (single writer).\nPostgres uses FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED so multiple\nworkers never claim the same row.
